/T (One method of measuring the affordability of housing is to study the ratio of house prices to average earnings, which by the end of 2015, had reached 5:1. This exceeded the ratio of approximately 4:1 during the housing boom of the late 1980s, evidence that the housing market is in danger of overheating.)
