781 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (announced. One reason for the rise in house prices has been the increased number of buy to let investors, who purchase property as an investment which they then let out on the private rental market. As well as removing tax relief on mortgage interest payments, the Chancellor introduced a 3% additional stamp duty rate on any property bought as a buy to let or second home. This was in addition to the stamp duty already charged on the purchase of residential property. These reforms were designed to reduce significantly the incentives to invest in this market and prevent further upward pressure on house prices.)
/E (announced. One reason for the rise in house prices has been the increased number of buy to let investors, who purchase property as an investment which they then let out on the private rental market. As well as removing tax relief on mortgage interest payments, the Chancellor introduced a 3% additional stamp duty rate on any property bought as a buy to let or second home. This was in addition to the stamp duty already charged on the purchase of residential property. These reforms were designed to reduce significantly the incentives to invest in this market and prevent further upward pressure on house prices.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
